## Goal

Prove that structured stories improve real behavioral questions and prevent future schema, embedding, routing, or prompt changes from silently returning generic recommendations or no result.

## Baseline regression to lock

Record the current failure mode as a regression case:

- “Can you tell me about a time Marcos demonstrated great leadership skills?” currently ranks recommendation excerpts and does not retrieve the Xogito experience story when restricted to experience sources.
- Similar natural phrasings such as “Tell me about a time Marcos led through a difficult client situation” and “How did Marcos recover a frustrated client account?” currently fall below the consumer relevance floor.

The milestone must make natural phrasing succeed through the correct story path without lowering the relevance floor.

## Competency coverage matrix

Create a committed matrix mapping every controlled behavioral competency used by the authored corpus to:

- at least one natural recruiter-style query;
- the expected story source id or ids, explicit `any`/`all` semantics when several are listed, and an optional preferred source;
- the expected deterministic tool route;
- whether semantic discovery is also expected;
- the agent answer assertions.

No controlled behavioral competency may ship without an eval. Retrieval facets, technologies, vendors, contexts, and outcomes are not competencies and do not independently require one eval each. Cover wording variants such as:

- leadership and leading without formal authority;
- ownership and taking responsibility;
- difficult stakeholders and rebuilding trust;
- disagreement or conflict;
- ambiguity and changing requirements;
- mentoring and onboarding;
- failure, mistake, or learning;
- prioritization and trade-offs;
- technical leadership and decision making;
- teamwork and cross-functional collaboration.

Only retain tags and cases supported by real authored stories. Retrieval fixtures must use the owner-approved minimized tags from #290 and must not reintroduce removed competency duplicates or synonym clusters to improve scores.

## Authoring-question migration and leakage boundary

The approved retrieval questions authored in #290 are candidate eval inputs, not `CareerStory` fields and not indexed source text. Do not convert all authored questions automatically into golden cases.

Implement the locked 38-case initial manifest below. It remains within the approved 35–45 case budget and provides:

- at least one query targeting each authored story;
- coverage for every controlled behavioral competency;
- a useful balance of exact and fuzzy formulations;
- a small set of deliberately cross-cutting questions;
- honest absent-topic coverage, including the recorded competing-priorities and immovable-deadline gaps;
- additional absent topics where the corpus genuinely has no evidence.

