- `exact`: may deliberately reuse names, technologies, companies, or phrases present in indexed story content and acts as a retrieval-plumbing sanity check;
- `fuzzy`: natural recruiter wording whose complete normalized formulation must not appear in any indexed story chunk;
- `cross-cutting`: deliberately expects evidence from several source records rather than treating several possible examples as interchangeable;
- `absent-topic`: requires no result above the calibrated relevance floor.

